#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049773 :topic/difficulty 1.4866534924833008 :topic/id #uuid "124fce70-48dc-5897-8dfb-8d65e4d68415" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059662 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059493 :question/id #uuid "4cd24c10-1838-5f4b-ac88-cfbfc2ec4c21" :question/math-academy-id "e-3518" :question/problem "Express $\\sin\\left(x - 30^{\\circ} \\right )$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u\\cos v - \\cos u\\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=30^{\\circ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{30}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69e91ce7-259a-5a11-bb79-7e6ad7ea86d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059663 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059494 :question/id #uuid "7341638b-3c0f-5c10-8b7d-a2c313607bed" :question/math-academy-id "e-3519" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y) = \\sin x\\cos y - \\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ and $y = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "213eda96-c41d-5361-9da9-8349617014f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059820 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059627 :question/id #uuid "0ce71d86-7470-5d53-ac94-20b473889dee" :question/math-academy-id "e-9983" :question/problem "Express $\\sin\\left(x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v) = \\sin{u}\\cos{v} + \\cos{u}\\sin{v}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u = x$ and $v = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b12a7b7-1df3-5203-934e-8820604de3de" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :topic/math-academy-id 270 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048362} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048430} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048672} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049136} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049850}] :topic/title "The Sum and Difference Formulas for Sine"}]}
